## Backlog Governance

- Tasks are added to this file only with explicit approval.
- Status transitions are tracked here in real time.
- IN_PROGRESS tasks must have a branch, an owner, and a task start time.
- BLOCKED tasks must document the blocker.
- REVIEW tasks must have acceptance evidence attached.
- DONE tasks must have a merged PR or explicit closure reason.
- Never delete task entries; archive completed ones by moving to a done section.

## Priority Definitions

| Priority | Meaning |
|---|---|
| P0 | Critical — blocks all dependent work |
| P1 | High — targeted for current iteration |
| P2 | Medium — scheduled but not urgent |
| P3 | Low — backing up for reference |
| P4 | Deprioritized — may be removed |

## Status Definitions

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| TODO | Approved and queued |
| IN_PROGRESS | Active implementation |
| BLOCKED | Waiting on external dependency |
| REVIEW | Awaiting acceptance decision |
| DONE | Completed and merged |

